<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fianarantsoa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fianarantsoa is a city in the southern highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> and the main town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/betsileo">Betsileo</a> region. It was founded in 1830 by the Merina queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-i">Ranavalona I</a> as an administrative centre to control the conquered Betsileo, and it became a centre of education, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and wine-making. A railway links it to Manakara on the east coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fianarantsoa.jpg" alt="Fianarantsoa" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HoneyGaLe · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_globale_de_la_ville_Fianarantsoa_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
